<section class="panel">
  <h2>What no connector can give you</h2>
  <p class="fine"><b>Seats.</b> SaaS utilisation needs active seats, and an
  invoice does not contain them: they come from your identity provider. That
  stays a file on purpose.</p>
  <p class="fine"><b>Memory.</b> No cloud reports guest memory without an agent
  in the guest: not AWS, not GCP, not Azure. CPU is free and agentless
  everywhere; memory needs the CloudWatch Agent, the Ops Agent or the Azure
  Monitor Agent. That is why the utilisation page states its coverage instead of
  claiming the whole estate.</p>
  <p class="fine"><b>Per-request AI cost.</b> Neither CUR nor FOCUS carries a
  per-request line: they aggregate by usage type over an hour or a day. Bedrock
  invocation logs are the only place a single call's tokens and its caller
  appear, and they are off by default.</p>
  <p class="fine"><b>FOCUS does not cover tokens yet.</b> FOCUS 1.4, ratified
  2026-06-04, has no AI token columns; surfacing model identity and token
  consumption is scoped for 1.5. AWS ships FOCUS 1.2 tables, and no model
  provider publishes FOCUS at all, so AI spend is normalised here by hand from
  each provider's own usage report.</p>
</section>
